# PlugV Launch Safety Rule

- Treat PlugV as an independent India-focused EV information platform; never imply government or manufacturer endorsement.
- Do not publish a vehicle, charger, price, launch, range, feature, availability or charging claim without a traceable source, verification date and honest confidence label.
- Never convert an estimate, fallback route, model output or partial source into an official/live fact.
- Use only PlugV-owned, generated, commissioned or explicitly licensed visual assets. Record every public asset in the asset-rights register.
- Preserve privacy-by-design: minimise personal data, obtain user action before location access, document external processors and never log secrets or sensitive user input.
- Protect every mutation/admin path with server-side authorization. Validate and bound all API inputs.
- Avoid unsupported “best”, “official”, “guaranteed”, “live” and superlative claims.
- Before completion run `npm run audit:release`. Do not describe a change as launch-ready when the command fails.
- Any legal/compliance conclusion requires qualified Indian counsel; record unresolved review items as launch blockers.

